{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Then HaShem will dispossess all these nations from before you.</b> The nearby ones, and afterwards: 'all the place where the sole of your foot treads' — and those are the far-off ones. Therefore the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said concerning David, peace be upon him, that he acted not in order and not according to the command of the Torah, for at first he conquered the far-off ones — and they are Aram Tzovah and Aram Naharayim, which are far from the Land — and afterwards he conquered the nearby ones. And for this reason they said: 'the conquest of an individual, its name is not conquest' — they called it 'the conquest of an individual' because the six myriad were not there; and they said 'its name is not conquest' for the matter of the sanctity of the Land regarding tithes and the sabbatical year of lands, from the Torah, but only rabbinically. And Aram Tzovah is Suryia; thus the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in the Sifrei."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:41.668286108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}